        {
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "content1",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "text-align": "left",
              "font-family": "'Oswald', sans-serif",
              "googleLink": "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Oswald:400,300,700",
              "color": "#000000"
            },
            "UL": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "font-family": "'Oswald', sans-serif",
              "googleLink": "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Oswald:400,300,700",
              "color": "#000000"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "content1-5u",
          "_params": {
            "paddingTop": "1",
            "paddingBottom": "1",
            "bgColor": "#ffffff"
          },
          "text": "<p>We use all new <b>GM Blocks</b> as the base foundation and meticulously machine each engine to ensure both performance and longevity. We can custom build our short blocks to work with your heads and can recommend compression ratios and custom camshafts to meet your hp goals.<br></p><p><br></p><ul><li>All new parts from <b>GM, Callies and Mahle</b><br></li></ul><ul><li>Balanced and Blueprinted<br></li></ul><ul><li>Each Engine Custom Built to Order<br></li></ul>",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "content1",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "text-align": "left",
              "font-family": "'Oswald', sans-serif",
              "googleLink": "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Oswald:400,300,700",
              "color": "#000000"
            },
            "UL": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "font-family": "'Oswald', sans-serif",
              "googleLink": "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Oswald:400,300,700",
              "color": "#000000"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "content1-5v",
          "_params": {
            "paddingTop": "1",
            "paddingBottom": "2",
            "bgColor": "#ffffff"
          },
          "text": "<p>We offer all new builds in both short and long block form as well complete turn key packages that comes dyno tested and tuned. All of our engines are built to order which allows you to customize the power level to suit your needs.</p><p><br></p><p>\n</p><p>\n</p><p>Optional parts include:</p><ul><li>Custom Cams</li></ul><ul><li>Aftermarket Cylinder heads and Intake Manifolds</li></ul><ul><li>Custom Valve Covers</li><li>Stainless Steel Headers</li><li>Billet Front Runner Kits</li><li>Stand Alone EFI Systems</li><li>Performance Transmissions</li></ul>",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_styles": {
            ".mbr-section-title, .mbr-section-subtitle": {
              "text-align": "center"
            },
            ".mbr-section-title": {
              "color": "#8c8c8c"
            },
            ".mbr-section-title SPAN": {
              "font-size": "46px"
            }
          },
          "_params": {
            "showMeta": false,
            "paddingTop": "3",
            "paddingBottom": "3",
            "bgColor": "#000000"
          },
          "title": "<span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">LSx Crate Engines</span>",
          "meta": "By John Smith posted July 20, 2016",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "header3",
          "_anchor": "header3-19t",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "paddingTop": "2",
            "paddingBottom": "2",
            "bgColor": "#ffffff"
          },
          "text": "<p>When it's time to install a new motor, what's better than a proven Chevy LSx engine? Aluminum block Gen III and IV engines that bear the LS designation are compact, lightweight and can make lots of power. An LSx crate engine is the fastest, easiest and most reliable way of getting your car ready for street or strip.<br></p><p>\n</p><p><br></p><p><b>Understand the LSx Engine Family</b></p><p>The LS1 debuted in 1997 and was soon followed by the stronger and more powerful LS6. 2005 saw a switch to the Gen IV engine, starting with the 6.0 liter LS2. Then came the 5.3 liter FWD LS4, the 7.0 liter LS7, the 6.2 liter LS3 and the blown LS9.\n</p><p>\n</p><p><br></p><p><b>LS1 or LSx?\n</b></p><p>There's an LSx crate engine to suit every need, from daily driver to rubber-burning hot rod. For rebuilding an older car, many owners choose an LS1 crate engine. This often saves time and money as many of the auxiliary components can be moved.\n</p><p>\n</p><p><br></p><p><b>Looking for an LSx Engine for Sale?\n</b></p><p>At Golen Engine, we offer many variants of the classic LSx. These range from the LS1 crate engine up to the LS3. We sell them in short block, long block and complete engines. \n</p><p>\n</p><p><br></p><p><b>Here's an overview.\n</b></p><p>\n</p><ul><li>Short Block LSx: You get a new GM block and crank, along with forged steel rods and Speed Pro pistons, plus American-made bearings and rings. The whole assembly is balanced for less vibration and longer main bearing life. It’s also blueprinted to extract as much power as possible while ensuring the engine will last.\n</li></ul><p>\n</p><ul><li>Long Block LSx: Take the short block and add a cam and fully built-up heads.\n</li></ul><p>\n</p><ul><li>Complete LSx Engine: This gets the appropriate intake plus the ignition system and all the covers. Simply mate it up to the trans, hook up the hoses and you're good to go.\n</li></ul><p>\n</p><p><br></p><p><b>The Golen Engine Difference\n</b></p><p>If you're trying to find a good LS1 engine for sale, there are many places to look. Don't cut corners when you're replacing the motor, invest in a quality LSx engine. Talk to us. We can supply an LSx crate engine that delivers power and performance for years to come. Call us today.\n</p><p><br></p>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "content1",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "text-align": "left",
              "color": "#000000"
            },
            "UL": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "color": "#000000"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "content1-19s",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_styles": {
            ".mbr-section-title, .mbr-section-subtitle": {
              "text-align": "center"
            },
            ".mbr-section-title": {
              "color": "#8c8c8c",
              "font-size": "46px"
            },
            ".mbr-section-subtitle": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "color": "#ffffff"
            },
            ".mbr-section-title SPAN": {
              "font-size": "46px"
            }
          },
          "_params": {
            "showMeta": true,
            "paddingTop": "4",
            "paddingBottom": "4",
            "bgColor": "#000000"
          },
          "title": "<span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">LSx TESTIMONIALS</span>",
          "meta": "What our Customers say",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "header3",
          "_anchor": "header3-lj",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "showTitle": false,
            "showText": true,
            "showButtons": false,
            "inverse": true,
            "imageSize": 50,
            "paddingTop": "1",
            "paddingBottom": "1",
            "bgImageRadio": false,
            "bgImage": "@PROJECT_PATH@/assets/images/dsc-5467.jpg",
            "parallax": true,
            "bgColorRadio": true,
            "bgColor": "#fff",
            "bgVideoRadio": false,
            "bgVideo": {
              "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uNCr7NdOJgw"
            },
            "overlay": true,
            "overlayColor": "#fff",
            "overlayOpacity": "0.8"
          },
          "media": {
            "image": {
              "active": true,
              "width": 1400,
              "src": "@PROJECT_PATH@/assets/images/camaro-5-300x225.jpg",
              "link": "",
              "alt": "Terry & Kristie Cramer",
              "title": "Terry & Kristie Cramer"
            },
            "video": {
              "src": "https://www.youtube.com/embed/Tq7p44IA-1U",
              "aspectratio": "16:9",
              "autoplay": false,
              "loop": false
            },
            "iconFont": {
              "class": "mbr-iconfont mbr-iconfont-msg-box5",
              "link": "",
              "size": 0
            }
          },
          "title": "SOLID COLOR INTRO WITH IMAGE",
          "text": "Chad, \n<br>\n<br>I just wanted to give you an update on the boosted LSX 427 engine we bought from you. With a 76mm turbo @ 19lbs of boost and some fuel modification in our 2010 camaro it is making 830 hp at the tires and 824 ft lbs of torque at the tires on pump gas only. \n<br>\n<br>Thank you for all of your help, \n<br>Terry &amp; Kristie Cramer",
          "buttons": "<a data-app-btn=\"true\" class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://mobirise.com\">MORE</a>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "msg-box5",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
              "text-align": "left",
              "color": "#000000"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "msg-box5-lk",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "showTitle": false,
            "showText": true,
            "showButtons": false,
            "inverse": true,
            "imageSize": 50,
            "paddingTop": "1",
            "paddingBottom": "1",
            "bgImageRadio": false,
            "bgImage": "@PROJECT_PATH@/assets/images/enginewf.jpg",
            "parallax": true,
            "bgColorRadio": true,
            "bgColor": "#efefef",
            "bgVideoRadio": false,
            "bgVideo": {
              "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uNCr7NdOJgw"
            },
            "overlay": true,
            "overlayColor": "#ffffff",
            "overlayOpacity": "0.8"
          },
          "media": {
            "image": {
              "active": true,
              "width": 1400,
              "src": "@PROJECT_PATH@/assets/images/gary-rosen-1-300x200.jpg",
              "link": "",
              "alt": "Gary Rosen",
              "title": "Gary Rosen"
            },
            "video": {
              "src": "https://www.youtube.com/embed/Tq7p44IA-1U",
              "aspectratio": "16:9",
              "autoplay": false,
              "loop": false
            },
            "iconFont": {
              "class": "mbr-iconfont mbr-iconfont-msg-box5",
              "link": "",
              "size": 0
            }
          },
          "title": "SOLID COLOR INTRO WITH IMAGE",
          "text": "I just wanted to let you know how pleased I am with my engine that the crew at Golen Engine built for me. The motor is an LS2 in a 2005 Corvette. Chad and his crew did an excellent job rebuilding this engine that had previously suffered a complete meltdown at the hands of a completely incompetant, I use this term loosely, mechanic. The engine was returned to me as promised, and running like a top. The motor was stroked to a 402ci from the stock 364ci. Chad’s expertise with these motors is exemplary. I chose his shop because all the work is done under one roof, this became exceptionally important when it came to trying to save my original aftermarket heads which had a leak, not all shops have a vacuum tank and would be able to diagnose this issue, at least none of my local shops could have. The heads had to ultimately be replaced, but the company that manufactured them did send me a new set free of charge. Chad was able to pinpoint the leak showing it was a manufacturers defect, something that could not have been done by a lesser shop, and I would not received a pair of new heads. My local shop said to just sell them for scrap. \n<br>\n<br>I recently returned from my first road trip in the car through the southeast, where the temperatures ranged from the mid 80’s to the low 90’s, the engine performed effortlesy. The engine was dyno tuned here in Florida. The tuner was also equally impressed with the results of the build. He told me that it is extremely rare to see an engine pull within 1/2hp on four successive power pulls. The tuning was done in early August where the temperatures were in the upper 80’s. The tuner I have been using for years is well known, running a tuning school where he instructs tuner’s throughout the U.S and abroad, so he’s seen quite a few engines. The engine put down 516hp and 486ftLbs of tq at the wheels. Both the tuner and Chad believe there is still about 15-20hp available if I upgrade to the 102mm Throttle body and larger headers. I am currently running a ported 90mm throttle body and 1 3/4 inch headers. Unfortunately this requires more $$, so we’ll see next year. \n<br>\n<br>I am looking forward to many years of enjoyment out of this motor. I’m hoping to do a few track days this fall so I can really have some fun and see what it’ll do. The car easily breaks loose in first and second, stationary and rolling, my wife is not too fond of this trait, I’ve been telling her that the seat is loose and I need to tighten it up! Not sure she believes me. \n<br>\n<br>Anyway, I am a completely satisfied customer. \n<br>Gary Rosen",
          "buttons": "<a data-app-btn=\"true\" class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://mobirise.com\">MORE</a>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "msg-box5",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
              "color": "#000000",
              "text-align": "left"
            }
