        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "paddingTop": "1",
            "paddingBottom": 1,
            "bgColor": "#fff"
          },
          "text": "<b>LS Build Process</b>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "content1",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
              "text-align": "center",
              "font-size": "25px",
              "font-family": "'Oswald', sans-serif",
              "googleLink": "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Oswald:400,300,700"
            },
            "DIV": {
              "text-align": "center",
              "font-size": "30px"
            },
            "B": {
              "font-size": "36px"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "content1-ls",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "paddingTop": 1,
            "paddingBottom": 1,
            "bgColor": "#fff"
          },
          "text": "<p>Here we are building a 502ci LS Chevy engine which features the RHS Aluminum Race Block, this build will make between 800-850hp when all finished. Follow our process below to see how we build this beast!!<br></p>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "content1",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "text-align": "center"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "content1-lt",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "showText": false,
            "paddingTop": "1",
            "paddingBottom": "1",
            "bgColor": "#fff"
          },
          "media": {
            "image": {
              "active": true,
              "src": "@PROJECT_PATH@/assets/images/1-1.jpg",
              "width": 1400,
              "link": "",
              "alt": "Sunnen SV-15 Cylinder hone",
              "title": "Sunnen SV-15 Cylinder hone"
            },
            "video": {
              "src": "https://www.youtube.com/embed/Tq7p44IA-1U"
            }
          },
          "text": "Create awesome mobile-friendly websites. No coding and free.",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "image2",
          "_anchor": "image2-lq",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "paddingTop": 1,
            "paddingBottom": 1,
            "bgColor": "#fff"
          },
          "text": "<p>We use our Sunnen SV-15 Cylinder hone to get the cylinders round and straight as possible. Here we are using a torque plate that is aluminum to simulate the aluminum head that we will run on this engine. This machine allows us to set the cross hatch for different ring sets, here we are setting it for a stainless steel top ring.</p>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "content1",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "text-align": "center"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "content1-lx",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
