        {
          "_styles": {
            ".mbr-section-title, p": {
              "color": "#fff"
            },
            ".mbr-section-title": {
              "font-size": "60px"
            },
            ".mbr-section-title SPAN": {
              "font-size": "60px"
            },
            ".lead P": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "color": "#ffffff",
              "text-align": "left"
            }
          },
          "_params": {
            "showTitle": true,
            "showText": true,
            "showButton": false,
            "paddingTop": "3",
            "paddingBottom": "1",
            "bgImageRadio": true,
            "bgImage": "@PROJECT_PATH@/assets/images/402-550hp-3.jpg",
            "parallax": true,
            "bgColorRadio": false,
            "bgColor": "#F2F2F2",
            "bgVideoRadio": false,
            "bgVideo": {
              "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uNCr7NdOJgw"
            },
            "overlay": true,
            "overlayColor": "#000000",
            "overlayOpacity": "0.4"
          },
          "title": "<span style=\"font-weight: normal;\"><i>From a C6 Corvette to </i></span><br><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\"><i>a </i></span><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\"><i>1st Gen Camaro\n</i></span>",
          "text": "<p>Our entire line of Chevy LS engines can be custom built to be a direct bolt in for any vehicle so weather you have a GM car that came from the factory with a LS based engine or you have a early hot rod that you would like to retro fit we have you covered. Check out the options below  and keep in mind that we offer full engine custom builds so if you do not see what you are looking for just ask.</p>",
          "button": "<a data-app-btn=\"true\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\" href=\"https://mobirise.com\">SEE ALL TEMPLATES</a>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "msg-box8",
          "_anchor": "msg-box8-1dh",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_styles": {
            ".mbr-section-title, .mbr-section-subtitle": {
              "text-align": "center"
            },
            ".mbr-section-title": {
              "font-size": "46px",
              "color": "#000000"
            }
          },
          "_params": {
            "showMeta": false,
            "paddingTop": "2",
            "paddingBottom": "2",
            "bgColor": "#fff"
          },
          "title": "LS7 427ci 650hp Complete Engine Upgrades",
          "meta": "By John Smith posted July 20, 2016",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "header3",
          "_anchor": "header3-1dj",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "paddingTop": "2",
            "paddingBottom": "2",
            "bgColor": "#ffffff"
          },
          "text": "<p>Our 427ci 650hp LS7 Engine can be built to be a direct replacement for the Z06 Corvette with its factory dry sump oiling or we can build it with a wet sump oil pump and put into any hot rod. This engine makes great torque and upper end hp with a redline of 7000 rpm you will be sure to impress at any car show. Using good performance long tube header that has 1 7/8” primary tubes and a 3.5” collector is recommend. This engine works best with a 3500 rpm stall or any manual transmission and a 3.73 gear or lower, you can check out our offerings from RPM Transmission below.</p>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "content1",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "text-align": "left"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "content1-1dk",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
