              "color": "#000000"
            }
          },
          "_params": {
            "showMeta": false,
            "paddingTop": "2",
            "paddingBottom": "2",
            "bgColor": "#fff"
          },
          "title": "RHS LS7 502ci 800hp Complete Engine Upgrades",
          "meta": "By John Smith posted July 20, 2016",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "header3",
          "_anchor": "header3-1f7",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "paddingTop": "2",
            "paddingBottom": "2",
            "bgColor": "#ffffff"
          },
          "text": "<p>Our 502ci RHS Engine is as big as it gets in the LS Engine world, making a whopping 800hp and close to 700 ft lbs of torque NA. It does require a really good flowing intake such as the Holley Hi Ram or the Performance Design TR in order to break the 800hp mark. We can build this engine to fit into any GM car that came with a LS based engine from the factory or set it up as a turn key package for a hot rod. Using good performance long tube header that has 2” primary tubes and a 3.5” collector is recommend. This engine works best with a 3500 rpm stall or any manual transmission and a 3.73 gear or lower, you can check out our offerings from RPM Transmission below.</p>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "content1",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "text-align": "left"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "content1-1f8",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
