        {
          "_params": {
            "paddingTop": "2",
            "paddingBottom": "2",
            "bgColor": "#ffffff"
          },
          "text": "<div><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">We offer restoration builds on both small and big block Ford engines and can offer stock or increased power levels. With our modern day machine shop we can properly machine your muscle car engine to perform better than it did new and we also offer a dyno break in service to ensure the engine is running properly and fully broken in before you start the install. We offer updates such as hyd roller camshaft, modern day Viton valve seals and hardened exhaust seats for use with unleaded fuels to name a few.</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><br></span></font></div><ul><li>Stroker Small Block Fords Available\n</li><li>FE Ford Restoration and Performance\n</li><li>Dyno Break In Service\n</li><li>Detail Painted Factory Color\n</li><li>Free Custom Quotes</li></ul>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "content1",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "text-align": "left",
              "font-family": "'Oswald', sans-serif",
              "googleLink": "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Oswald:400,300,700",
              "color": "#000000"
            },
            "UL": {
              "font-size": "20px",
              "font-family": "'Oswald', sans-serif",
              "googleLink": "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Oswald:400,300,700",
              "color": "#000000"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "content1-1js",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "paddingTop": 1,
            "paddingBottom": "2",
            "bgColor": "#fff"
          },
          "text": "<h1>Ford Muscle Car Engines\n</h1><div>\n</div><div>Classic Fords came with some legendary engines — the Boss 302, for example, or the 428 Cobra Jet. For their time, they made lots of power and torque. Yet by today's standards, they're just a little ordinary. If you want more grunt, it's time to find out what's possible in the world of Ford muscle car engines. Here at Golen Engine, we have stock and upgraded Ford performance engines for sale, and that includes Ford small block stroker engines.</div><div><br></div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><h5><b>Small Blocks, Big Blocks and Strokers\n</b></h5><div>A restoration or hot-rod build engine will give your Galaxy, Mustang or Torino a new lease on life. Same for your Fairlane or Cougar. You could pull the motor and spend forever on a rebuild, or you could come to Golen Engine.</div><div><br></div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>We can build the 396ci stroker or 427 FE side oiler of your dreams. You want updates like a hydraulic roller camshaft, Viton valve seals and hardened exhaust seats? Yes, we can do that. Once it's built, we'll test and tune it on one of our SuperFlow SF-902 engine dynos.</div><div><br></div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>Two big benefits of our muscle car engines are speed and reliability. By speed, we mean you'll be back on the road in less time — especially if you take advantage of our break-in service. As for reliability, we use only high-quality American-made parts and we put a three-year warranty on every engine we build.</div><div><br></div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><h5><b>Understanding Ford Muscle Car Engines\n</b></h5><div>Blue Oval enthusiasts say Ford V8s ruled the 1960s, and it's hard to argue. Taking over from the “Y-block” at the start of the decade, the Ford-Edsel “FE” — with its 4.63-inch bore spacing — just grew and grew in displacement.</div><div><br></div><div> \n</div><div>\n</div><div>Technically somewhere between a small block and big block, many say the FE was at its best as the 427ci “Medium Riser” engine found in a limited number of Galaxies, Fairlanes and Comets. There's also the 428 Cobra Jet variant of 1968. What an engine! Blessed was the Mach 1, Cougar or Fairlane Torino that received this beauty!</div><div><br></div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><h5><b>About the Ford 351\n</b></h5><div>There are two 351ci Ford V8s — the Windsor and the Cleveland. The Windsor is a small block that's been around forever, most recently as the 5.0. The Cleveland-built 351 however, was part of the 335-family produced between 1970 and ’74. With a stronger crank and larger ports, this is capable of higher rpms and more horsepower.</div><div><br></div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>Also noteworthy, a 351 strokes to 396ci. If Ford small block stroker crate engines are for you, talk to us!</div><div><br></div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><h5><b>Seeking Big Block Ford Engines for Sale?\n</b></h5><div>We can help. If you want small block Ford engines for sale, we build them, too. Learn more by calling <a href=\"tel:1-800-591-9171\" class=\"text-warning\">1-800-591-9171</a>. Alternatively, fill out our <a href=\"contact-us.html\" class=\"text-warning\">online form</a> and we’ll be in touch ASAP.</div>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "content1",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
              "font-size": "20px"
            },
            "H1": {
              "text-align": "center"
            },
            "DIV": {
              "font-size": "20px"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "content1-1m0",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3"
        },
